# Canonical author names.
#
# The first four commits were made before the repository-local git identity was
# set to a real name, so they record the GitHub handle "muhammad-asifkhan" while the later
# ones record "Muhammad Asif Khan". Same person, same address.
#
# A .mailmap normalises how git and most forges DISPLAY those names -- in
# `git log`, `git shortlog -sne`, and contributor lists -- without rewriting a
# single commit. Rewriting history to fix a display inconsistency would be a
# poor trade, and this file makes it unnecessary.
#
# Format:  Canonical Name <canonical@email>  Old Name <same@email>

Muhammad Asif Khan <asifcalm53@gmail.com> muhammad-asifkhan <asifcalm53@gmail.com>
